1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
(Instrumental music)
 
(Instrumental music)

2
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Dembaş, temaşevanên me yên hêja, temaşevanên me yên ezîz.
 
Good day, our valuable viewers, our dear viewers.

3
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Em hatin bi vîdyoyekî xweş û bi hêvî me hûn gî di nav xêr û
xweşiyê da bin.
 
We have come with a nice video and I hope you are all in
goodness and well-being.

4
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Silavên min ji gundê Celeme tevahî ra heye. Çil vir, û çil
xerîbiyê silavên min ji çûk û mezinên wan ra heye.
 
I send my greetings to the entire village of Jalama. To all
those here and those abroad, I send my greetings to their
young and old.

5
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Lê îro jî me xwest em berê xwe bidin navçeya Cindirêsê û bi
taybet jî, gundê Celeme.
 
But today we wanted to head to the Jinderes district, and
specifically, to the village of Jalama.

6
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Gundê Celeme dengê gundê ji dûr ve pir xweş e, lê carek min
derbasî nedîtin heta ev cara yekemîn e ku em derbasî gundê
Celeme bûn.
 
The fame of the village of Jalama is very beautiful from
afar, but I had never passed through it, this is the first
time we entered the village of Jalama.

7
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Gundê Celeme bi erdê xwe, bi bistanên xwe, bi xelkên wê, em
pir kesanan zê bikin dibêjin em ji Celeme ne.
 
The village of Jalama, with its land, its orchards, its
people, we meet many people who say they are from Jalama.

8
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Lê belê me îro jî xwest em zû rabin û em bi hev ra herin
derbasî gundê Celeme bin.
 
But today we wanted to get up early and together go and
enter the village of Jalama.

9
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Berî em dest bi vîdyoya xwe bikin, ez spasî her kesî dikim
li kêleka vê qenalê disekine, em bûn çil hezar ser YouTube.
 
Before we start our video, I thank everyone who stands by
this channel, we have reached forty thousand on YouTube.

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Û bi taybet li pêncî û sedî be.
 
And specifically for the fifty and a hundred percent.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
De naha jî bi me re bin ez û hûn, em ê bi hev re derbasî
gundê Celeme bin.
 
So now stay with us, you and I, together we will enter the
village of Jalama.

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:13,000
(Instrumental music plays)
 
(Instrumental music plays)

13
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, piştî em derbasî gundê Celeme
jî bûn, lê ji gundê Celeme jî berî em li nav gund bigerin,
em ê derbasî cîhekî bibin.
 
Yes, our valuable viewers, after we entered the village of
Jalama, but before we walk around the village of Jalama, we
will enter a place.

14
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Vê cihê jî pir bav û kalên me yê berê dikirin vê karê.
 
This place too, many of our forefathers used to do this
work.

15
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Ev malbat e, malbateke... bi taybetî ev kar di gund de, tenê
adeta ji gundê Celeme ye.
 
This family is, a family... specifically this work in the
village, is a tradition only from the village of Jalama.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Li cem gundekî delyûb heye. Gênim?
 
Is there a boiler in any village? For wheat?

17
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Dêre.
 
No.

18
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Vê karî jî heştê sal ne, ji heştê salî heya niha, bi vê karî
îhtîfaz kirine û bi vî karî radibin.
 
This work has been going on for eighty years, from eighty
years ago until now, they have preserved this work and
continue to do it.

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Naha jî werin bi me re, em bi hev ra bisekinin hela çiqas
kibar û delal çêkirine vê delîbê.
 
Now come with us, let's stand together and see how nicely
and beautifully they have made this boiler.

20
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Em derbasî gundê Celeme bûm, rastî ev e cara yekem e em
derbasî gundê Celeme dibin.
 
We entered the village of Jalama, truthfully this is the
first time we are entering the village of Jalama.

21
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Gundê Celeme min teweqi' nedikir, tebîetê gundê wisa xweş be
û pir kîbar be.
 
The village of Jalama, I did not expect the village's nature
to be so beautiful and very nice.

22
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:13,000
(Instrumental music plays)
 
(Instrumental music plays)

23
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Dembaş xalo, çawa yî baş î?
 
Good day uncle, how are you, are you well?

24
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Baş e, ehlen we sehlen.
 
Good, welcome.

25
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Saet xweş xwedê qewetê bide te da.
 
Good times, may God give you strength.

26
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Ehlen we sehlen, ser sera û ser çava.
 
Welcome, you are upon my head and eyes.

27
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Em pir kêfxweş in em vê karî dibînin. Xwedê quwetê bide te
dayê.
 
We are very happy to see this work. May God give you
strength mother.

28
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Em nas bikin, destpêkê...
 
Let's get to know you, first...

29
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Ez Ednan Yûsif Xelîl im. Gundê Celeme.
 
I am Adnan Yusuf Khalil. Village of Jalama.

30
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Em ji doze vî karî digerin, kar û barê bav û kalên me yê
berê, rehmêtî dikirin...
 
We have been doing this work for a long time, the work and
business of our ancestors in the past, the late ones used to
do it...

31
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Dûr e me destpê kir. Teb'en berê ne wisa bû. Me ji tiştên
ecêb kirin, hedîs kirin.
 
We started it a long time ago. Of course it wasn't like this
before. We made wonderful things, modernized it.

32
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Ev teqrîben bav û kalên me rehmêtî, sîh, sîh salî tê da
şixulîn.
 
For this, our late ancestors, worked in it for about thirty,
thirty years.

33
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Naha em jî teqrîben bîst û pênc, sîh û çar sal em jî tê de
dixebitin.
 
Now we also for about twenty-five, thirty-four years we have
been working in it as well.

34
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Vê karî wan ji bav û kalên xwe ra kirin, bes em dibînin we
tiştin tê da ecerlemiş kirin.
 
They inherited this work from their ancestors, but we see
you have modernized some things in it.

35
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Hawa ev kevirê me ê esarê zeytûnê ye. Bes me kir e ye bulxur
e.
 
Like this stone of ours is from an olive press. But we made
it for bulgur.

36
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Tiştên me tê da xeyirandin, kir e ye bulxur e.
 
We changed some things in it, made it for bulgur.

37
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Xalê Ednan beriya em derbasî cem te bin, em di rê de dihatin
ji me re xeber dan gotin gundên derdorê Celeme gişk tên cem
te.
 
Uncle Adnan, before we came to you, we were coming on the
way, they told us that all the villages around Jalama come
to you.

38
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Erê hawa ji qeta'eya vî alî gişk tên cem me. Gel cem me ne.
 
Yes, like from this sector all come to us. People are with
us.

39
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Me jî xwest em derbasî cem te bin, em te nas bikin, û pişt
re em li ser...
 
We also wanted to come to you, get to know you, and then
on...

40
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Xalê Ednan çend saetan ew genim tê kelandin, heta weha
dibe... Naha vir tenê qaşir radibe ne wisa?
 
Uncle Adnan, how many hours is that wheat boiled until it
becomes like this... Now here only the peel comes off,
right?

41
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Hawa hem yê bulxur heye, û hem yê genim heye. Genim me'neyê
şorbeyê ye.
 
Well there is one for bulgur, and one for wheat. Wheat means
for soup.

42
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Ew ya kuta ye û deran ev e... Bes ev e em qeliq radikin ev
e, dibe bulxur û sêmîs ê derdikeve.
 
That's the crushed one and the output is this... But this
one, we take off the husk and it becomes bulgur and semolina
comes out.

43
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Naha ko merheleya selef, genimê xwe tînin şûştin heye. Piştî
genim hat kelandin, tînin cem te...
 
Now like the previous stage, bringing their wheat there is
washing. After the wheat is boiled, they bring it to you...

44
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Dê destpêkê dikelînin, ba'dî kelandinê tînin li vê derê,
qalik radibe, ji vê derê derdikeve...
 
First they boil it, after boiling they bring it here, the
husk is removed, it comes out of here...

45
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Paşê diçe wê derê tenşîf e, derdixe hêsîran. De ev der
derdixe, hêmî meanê gîrmiyê derdixe, hêm me'nê hevîrê
derdixe.
 
Then it goes there to dry, it takes out the impurities. Then
this place takes it out, it takes out both the crushed parts
and the flour.

46
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Naha di vir da teqrîben wê çiqas bimîne ev genimê, ev qalik?
 
Now here approximately how long will this wheat, this husk
stay?

47
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Hawa saetekê dimîne. Saet, saet û nîvek dimîne hasabê
pirbûn, hindikbûna wî.
 
Well it stays for an hour. It stays for an hour, an hour and
a half depending on the amount, if it's a lot or a little.

48
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Ba'dî ku ew anîn, bi hev da dibe. Çi derê?
 
After they bring it, it's mixed together. Where to?

49
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Bi xwe xwediyê wê dibe. Sahibê wê ji binî de derdixe, dixe
nava torbeya xwe.
 
The owner himself takes it. The owner takes it out from
underneath and puts it in his sack.

50
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Baş e ew tilûra te tê de dixist?
 
Okay, that machine you put it in?

51
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Ew derdixe tenşîf e. Qalik de rê wê cîkî, tenê tê da tê.
 
It takes it out and dries it. The husk goes to one place,
the grain comes in.

52
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Qalikan di wê derê radihêjin, paşê darên hûr...
 
They collect the husks there, then small pieces of wood...

53
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Naha am dibînin li herêmê, yanî tenê tu vî karî dikî?
 
Now we see in the region, I mean are you the only one doing
this work?

54
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Hene... hene. Em çar cîh bûn, li Cindirêsê hebû, li Bafilorê
hebû, û li Qîbarê hebû, û li Şiyê heye.
 
There are... there are. We were four places, there was one
in Jinderes, there was one in Baflore, and there was one in
Qibar, and there is one in Shiye.

55
00:05:51,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Hene, teqrîben evî ne... Lê belê ew dawer ne man, her gundek
hebû. Berê dawer dikirin, bi garanê da.
 
There are, approximately these... But those cattle-powered
ones are no more, every village had them. In the past they
used cattle, they ran it with a herd.

56
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Berê jî naha kî ne bibin, ev qalik a bav û kalên me yê tê
radibûn?
 
In the past, who were doing this, this husk removing that
our ancestors used to do?

57
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Erê, lê destpêkê hawa hîn, curn hebûn. Dikirin, saqî bi
destan dihat kutakirin, şebabek di kutan.
 
Yes, but in the beginning, they were still using mortars.
They used to do it, it was crushed by hand, youth used to
crush it.

58
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Piştî wê, em kê ne bibin li her gundekî delyûbek hebû.
 
After that, there was a boiler in every village.

59
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Hebû.
 
There was.

60
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Heywan tînan di wê delûbe ve girê didan û digerandin. Naha
pêşketiye zeman...
 
They used to bring animals and tie them to that mill and
spin it. Now time has progressed...

61
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Naha li berî li ser motor e, li ser motorê me zêde kiriye.
 
Now it's running on a motor, we have added a motor to it.

62
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Destê te sax bin, karekî pîroz e, karekî bi şeref e, ev
karekî ji me re ye em serbilind in bi vê karê hawa em kî ne
bibin tûrasa...
 
Bless your hands, it is a sacred work, an honorable work,
this is a work for us, we are proud of this work like this,
we are continuing the heritage...

63
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Ev tûras e û her miletek edet û teqalîdên xwe heye, ev edet
û teqalîd heta di xwarina miletê da... yanî adet û teqalîd û
xwarina xwe bitûnî.
 
This is heritage and every nation has its customs and
traditions, these customs and traditions even in the food of
the nation... I mean, customs and traditions and their food
entirely.

64
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Naha li di derê wan kî napirşirîne dernakeve.
 
Now in that place, they don't peel it off, it doesn't come
out.

65
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Ji wê re hinarê tê derbekê dihêlin, da bi qalok dihêlin, ev
ê me jî berê da e, em... em tenê qaşilên derdixin paşî kî
dikelînin.
 
For that they leave the pomegranate for a bit, they leave it
with the peel, this one of ours is also from the past, we...
we only take the peels off, then they boil it.

66
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Di ser vî tiştî jî, meseleyeke çûçik e heye, berê kal pîran
digotin.
 
Besides this, there is a small matter, the elders used to
say in the past.

67
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

68
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Me keçek çûçik e ku dimeşî. Min go ev kepek xwerî ye, yanî
qalqî ser xêr tê te ne.
 
We had a small girl walking. I said this is a bran eater,
meaning the husk is coming on your goodness.

69
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Yanî am kênî dibin vî... ev jê vir derdibe.
 
So we see this... this comes out of here.

70
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Ew jê vedibe.
 
It comes out of it.

71
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Vî kepekê, ji çi tiştî re bi kêr tê, xalê Adnan?
 
What is this bran used for, Uncle Adnan?

72
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Tişta ewa ye, ewa yê bulxur yê bi kêr nayê.
 
That thing, that is for bulgur, it's not useful.

73
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Bes ê dên, ye bi kêr tê.
 
But the broken wheat one is useful.

74
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Ê dên ji çi ra yê bi kêr tê?
 
What is the broken wheat one used for?

75
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:44,000
E dên, ewa genim ne... ne hatî kelandin. Qalqî ser, elyaf
têda hene, ew ê elyaf ne ji nexweşî roviyan, ji devokan
re...
 
The broken wheat one, that wheat is not... not boiled. The
husk on top has fibers in it, those fibers are for
intestinal diseases, for animals...

76
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Di nava nan da elyaf tê danîn e, pirik hene dibin... menî
wek xweş e. Nexweşî...
 
Fiber is put in bread, many take it... it's like a good
cure. Illnesses...

77
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Em spasî te mezin dikin, spasdariya te, ji me re wext dît da
em vê kare te nas bikin û ji nêvî cîhanê gundiyan.
 
We thank you very much, thank you for finding time for us so
we could get to know this work of yours and from half the
world of the villagers.

78
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Walayî di deriyê me ji milet giş re vekirî ye.
 
By God, our door is open to all the people.

79
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Saet xweş.
 
Good times.

80
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Deriyê me înşala timî ê vekirî be.
 
Our door will hopefully always be open.

81
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Daxwaziya me jî ewe miletê me be... Înşala.
 
Our wish is also that our people be... God willing.

82
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Û înşala, zorê ku te jî ev kar diyar bike tu vî karî bidî...
 
And hopefully, as much as you can manifest this work, you
will pass it on...

83
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Înşela.
 
God willing.

84
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Saet xweş, xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Good times, may God be pleased with you.

85
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Sax bî, ehlen we sehlen biko.
 
Be healthy, welcome son.

86
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:29,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

87
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:35,000
(Music and singing starts)
 
(Music and singing starts)

88
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Hatim Efrînê, canê, hatim Efrînê, canê...
 
I came to Afrin, my dear, I came to Afrin, my dear...

89
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Çûm Efrînê, canê, çûm Efrînê, canê...
 
I went to Afrin, my dear, I went to Afrin, my dear...

90
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Çûm Efrînê, canê...
 
I went to Afrin, my dear...

91
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Niharî hene bar e, niharî hene bar e...
 
There are springs, it's raining, there are springs, it's
raining...

92
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Bûka li zêr e bimbarek, bûka li zêr e bimbarek...
 
The bride is wearing gold congratulations, the bride is
wearing gold congratulations...

93
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:28,000
(Music fades out)
 
(Music fades out)

94
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Berê gîyî saeta we xweş...
 
First of all, have a good time...

95
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Xwedê ji we razî be, saet xweş.
 
May God be pleased with you, good time.

96
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Qewetê bide we dayê.
 
May He give you strength mother.

97
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Em pir keyfxweş bîn em derbasî gundê Celeme bûn, em we nas
bikin.
 
We were very happy to enter the village of Jalama, to get to
know you.

98
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Em dixwazin we nas bikin, piştî vê em derbasî gundê xwe
bibin.
 
We want to get to know you, after this we will move on to
our village.

99
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Ez Huseyn ê Rifat im.
 
I am Huseyn of Rifat.

100
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Kekê Huseyn.
 
Brother Huseyn.

101
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Ez ji Hesenan im. Bes em ji vî gundî me.
 
I am from the Hesens. But we are from this village.

102
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Kekê Huseyn. Û dayîkê?
 
Brother Huseyn. And mother?

103
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Hecî ye...
 
It's Haji...

104
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Xalê me?
 
Our uncle?

105
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Hecî Înce me. Ji ereban e.
 
I am Haji Ince. From the Arabs.

106
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Hecî Înce? Ji Ereban.
 
Haji Ince? From the Arabs.

107
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Înce ye ereban a...
 
Ince of the Arabs...

108
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Ser xêrê be. Emrê te dirêj be xaltî.
 
May it be for the best. Long live, aunt.

109
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Yê te jî.
 
Yours as well.

110
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Kekê Husên em dizanin jina te xeberda naha. Mîsala camêr
ewên e li sûkê tê ye...
 
Brother Husên, we know your wife spoke just now. For
example, the gentleman is those who come to the market...

111
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Ew e sûkê ye, ahan.
 
That is the market's, yes.

112
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:16,000
We dest pê kirîye. Çend rojin we dest pê kirîne vî karî
dikin?
 
You have started. How many days have you been starting to do
this work?

113
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Welle ji evwaliya heştê da teqrîben...
 
Well, approximately since the beginning of the eighth
(month)...

114
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Destpêka meha heştê da.
 
In the beginning of the eighth month.

115
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Sûk çawa ye, îsal da meşê?
 
How is the market, is it moving this year?

116
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Hemdulilah. Rind e îsal, rind e... yanî, ji 150 û ji wir da,
heta 150 der e. Rind e, hemdulilah.
 
Praise be to God. It is good this year, it is good...
meaning, from 150 and from there on, it's around 150. It's
good, praise be to God.

117
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Ji mûzari'an ra, em dibên bila xêra xwe, xilas bikin...
 
For the farmers, we say let them benefit, finish it...

118
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Xwe xilas bikin, îsal...
 
Finish it, this year...

119
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Hemdulilah, şikur ji xwedê ra.
 
Praise be to God, thanks to God.

120
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Naha li vî derê we gî kom kirîne? Hûn dikin tûra, piştî wî?
 
Now, have you gathered all of it here? You put them in bags,
after that?

121
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Em gî dikin tûra, paşê dibin sûkê, ahan.
 
We put them all in bags, then take them to the market, yes.

122
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Wela, vî derê navê wê çi yê, we lê çandiye?
 
Well, what is the name of this place where you have planted?

123
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Em lê dibên Baxçe, baxçe, ahan.
 
We call it a garden (Baxçe), garden, yes.

124
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Çolê... hewşê... hewşa malê, hewşa malê.
 
The field... the yard... the house yard, the house yard.

125
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Celamê, em dibînin pir kes, gundên der û dorên têne cem we,
bi zêran re îsal da dibin... qase îsal te weha, mexrûf ne.
 
In Celamê, we see many people, from surrounding villages
coming to you, they are taking with gold this year...
especially this year you are known like this.

126
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Çima?
 
Why?

127
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Her, sûkên hal, kî dibîne, dibên evna îsotên Celamê ne.
 
Every current market, whoever sees them, says these are the
peppers of Celamê.

128
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Îsotên Celamê... Celamê ji gundê dinya yê pirrtir diçînin
îsotan...
 
The peppers of Celamê... Celamê plants more peppers than any
other village in the world...

129
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Û pir gundê der û dorên jî hene têne, şitlan cem we dibin...
yanî hûn... îsotan da mafxûf ne gundê Celamê.
 
And there are many surrounding villages coming, taking
seedlings from you... meaning you... in peppers, the village
of Celamê is well-known.

130
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Tiştek din jî, em dibînin, titûn... Gundê, di Mentiqê
Efrînê, pir titûn çandiye gundê Celamê ye.
 
Another thing we see, tobacco... The village, in the Afrin
region, that plants a lot of tobacco is the village of
Celamê.

131
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Gundê Celamê ye, rast e.
 
It is the village of Celamê, that's true.

132
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Hal, yanî, empêr da bin vê tiştê.
 
Currently, meaning, empires are under this thing.

133
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Çî, kekê Husên, ez diwazim hinekî di ser titûnê jî min ra
xeber de, hûn çawa tê diçînin, çawa tê radikin?
 
What, brother Husên, I want you to talk to me a bit about
the tobacco as well, how do you plant it, how do you harvest
it?

134
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Di meştelan da tê çandin, û xona, ser bestekê, tê kav e...
teqrîben dehe, pêncî, çaran, wê deran, em dikin erdê,
 
It is planted in nurseries, and then, on a plot, it's laid
down... approximately in the 10s, 50s, 40s, around there, we
put them in the ground,

135
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:42,000
...û em dikolin... paşê çil û yek rojê qut dibe, û em dibin
nêk ro, divê em li menşera bixin.
 
...and we dig... then for forty-one days it is cut, and we
take them half a day, we have to put them on the drying
rack.

136
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Naha, ba'ad e, şitlê genim bikekekî hêsane... belê, genim
divê titûn...
 
Now, after, a wheat seedling is a little bit easy... yes,
wheat needs tobacco...

137
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Ahan. Belê.
 
Yes. Yes.

138
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Belê gund da hişk dikin.
 
Yes, they dry them in the village.

139
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
... da em hişk dikin...
 
... we dry them...

140
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Sema(t) têkeve...
 
Poisoning enters it...

141
00:11:54,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Semat têkev e... menşera vediqe... em hişk dikin, paşê daxin
bar-xerbî... û em dikin baliyan, û radikin... xilas dibe
karê wî.
 
Poisoning enters it... it opens the drying rack... we dry
them, then take them down to the west side... and we put
them in bales, and remove them... its work is finished.

142
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Xilas dibe.
 
It is finished.

143
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:21,000
(Silence / ambient sounds)
 
(Silence / ambient sounds)

144
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Dayê te çawa xilas kir? Çawa yî?
 
Mother, how did you finish? How are you?

145
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Hemdûllah. Te xwar kirîne, ahan, welleh.
 
Praise be to God. You have eaten them, yes, by God.

146
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Xwezî te xwar kira! Te dît te çûne...
 
I wish you had eaten them! (laughing) You saw they have
gone...

147
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Karê me çû.
 
Our work went away.

148
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Em hatin, mala xwe da... gundê Celamê, maşelle, zor û ko...
jinên vê gundî giştî li der û van karê xwe dikin.
 
We came, to your house... the village of Celamê, amazing,
young and old... the women of this village all work outside
doing these jobs.

149
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Erê... pirr jî me dîtin maşallah, hûn heta naha jî, hûn bi
kar difikirin.
 
Yes... we have seen a lot, amazing, you even now, you think
about work.

150
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Sahetek baş... ez dixim hinekî ser pîrekên vê gundî, min ra
tenekî bêje... Çi karî radibin, çi karî dikin... yanî jiyana
wan çawa derbaz dibe?
 
Have a good time... I want to ask a little about the women
of this village, tell me a bit... What work do they get up
for, what work do they do... meaning, how does their life
pass?

151
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Pîrekên jî... emrê xwedê... helak e... radibin... heta roje
ava... radibin ji qijikê xwarinê... ji kiçikê ro radibin ji
qijikê xwarinê.
 
Women too... God's age... are exhausted... they get up...
until sunset... they get up since from a small meal... from
a small day they get up from a small meal.

152
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Û em kanin bibêjin...
 
And we can say...

153
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Em pîrekên vê gundî, nîvê gişt dikin... çi karê çolê be,
radibin, nexwarî, têkên jin...
 
We the women of this village, do half of everything...
whatever work in the field there is, they get up, without
eating, being women...

154
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Naka, naha, vê emrîşê, na... narine çolê. Ya mal da...
hatiye wekî naka, iyi... vê dikin. Çol... çol tin e naka...
narin çolê.
 
No, now, in this age, no... they don't go to the field.
Either at home... it has become like now, well... they do
this. Field... there is no field now... they don't go to the
field.

155
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Ê can kanin herin.
 
The young ones can go.

156
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Erê can dikin herin, herin, xwarinê... em mala digirin, da
erin... ev tişt...
 
Yes, the young ones do go, they go, food... we take care of
the house, so they can go... these things...

157
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ev tiştên pir xwaş, ma re be hevra. Em li vir dere çêlek
dibînin... ev tu wane, xaltî?
 
These very nice things, let's have them together. We see a
cow here... is this yours, aunt?

158
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Ê min e, ahan.
 
It's mine, yes.

159
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:48,000
(Ambient sounds/Silence)
 
(Ambient sounds/Silence)

160
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Naha, ev e... em didin e... çawa ye hûn didin e?
 
Now, this is... we milk it... how do you milk it?

161
00:13:51,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Çawa hûn didoşin... em dikelînin şîr... em dimeyînin dikin
mast... û em heger em nekin mast... em dermankekî dikinê...
dikin penîr.
 
How you milk it... we boil the milk... we ferment it and
make yogurt... and if we don't make yogurt... we put a
medicine in it... we make cheese.

162
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Ê, em lorkê çêdikin, ... lorkê ...
 
And, we make lorik (a type of cheese), ... lorik ...

163
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Penîr am jî xwe radikin pere. Lorke.
 
We also save cheese as money. Lorik.

164
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Li heyatî gundan wiha ye? Hinek pezê te kê hebe, ... çêlek
hebin, ... gihê...
 
Is this how village life is? If you have a few sheep, ...
some cows, ... grass...

165
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Pezê te kê hebe.
 
If you have a few sheep.

166
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Çêlek hebin, gihê te... pez te kê hebe... heta mirîşkê te kê
hebe... a gund avan... te kê wan avabike.
 
If you have cows, grass... if you have a few sheep... even
if you have a few chickens... ah these village things... you
should build them up.

167
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Tu we... çend çêl cem te ne, dayê?
 
You have... how many cows do you have, mother?

168
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Belkî welle, de sisê-çar pêne.
 
Maybe by God, there are three or four of them.

169
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Ê mezin e wane, a wan e ê şîr in.
 
Those big ones, those are the ones for milk.

170
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,000
U ev na jî çêlikê wan an e.
 
And these are their calves.

171
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Ej ji te kin e?
 
Are they yours?

172
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Xwedê risqê we bişîne. Û emrê te dirêj be xaltî... ta'atiyê
wan te hertişt şanî me dît...
 
May God send your provision. And long live, aunt... your
obedience, you showed us everything...

173
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Şîrê gund, kîjan wext da hişk dibe... naha heye şîr mast di
gund e.
 
Village milk, what time does it dry up... now there is milk
and yogurt in the village.

174
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Waxtanî wale ki bim kîjan mehê, hişk dibin... gulanê, çend
meha dibin, hişk dibin... ecêb. Ewa, ez nizanim, waleh...
 
The time, by God, which month, they dry up... May, in a few
months, they dry up... surprisingly. That, I don't know, by
God...

175
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:08,000
(Silence / ambient sounds)
 
(Silence / ambient sounds)

176
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Ta riya avê heye.
 
There is a water path.

177
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Eşbarî. (Eşbariyê dikin borî.)
 
Ashbari. (They make the Ashbari into a pipe.)

178
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:36,000
(Silence / ambient sounds)
 
(Silence / ambient sounds)

179
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Kekê Husên, ez dixwazim hinekî li ser gundê Celamê xebere
din... em derbas bûn... derbas bûn em... çiqas gund mezin
e...
 
Brother Husên, I want to talk a little bit about the village
of Celamê... we passed by... we passed by... how big is the
village...

180
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Gundê wê, dor e çi qas mal e?
 
Your village, roughly how many houses are there?

181
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Wale... mezin e... ser hezar û pêncsed mal ro heye.
 
By God... it is big... there are over one thousand and five
hundred houses.

182
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Ecêbe, ev gundê na kirin navçe?
 
Surprising, didn't they make this village a district?

183
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Wale... li ser esasê, kiribûn naçye (nahiye), bes... zû
morkî...
 
By God... fundamentally, they had made it a sub-district,
but... it was quickly sealed...

184
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Em kanin bibêjin gundê we bi naçê Cindirêsê ve girêdayî ye.
 
We can say your village is connected to the sub-district of
Jindires.

185
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Çiqas kîlometra, ji naçê Cindirêsê dûr e û çiqas kîlometra
ji Efrînê dûr e, teqrîben?
 
How many kilometers is it far from the sub-district of
Jindires and how many kilometers is it far from Afrin,
approximately?

186
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Ji Cindirêsê nehe kîlometra dûr e. Û ji Efrînê, teqrîben,
dehe haft-heşt kîlometra weha der e.
 
It is nine kilometers far from Jindires. And from Afrin,
approximately, about seventeen or eighteen kilometers around
there.

187
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Naha el vê erdê ve çandina na... I'timadê xwe pirçe dikin,
ser bîrê avê.
 
Now about planting in this land... They mostly rely on water
wells.

188
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Ah.
 
Yes.

189
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Bîrê avê, dê gundê de di çiqas metrî da derdikeve, Kekê
Husên?
 
Water wells, at how many meters do they come out in the
village, Brother Husên?

190
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Waleh... bîrê rûbarê derdikeve, dehe çil û, pêncî da
derdikeve... bas ekterî... pir bahrî hatin... em kolan cem
me.
 
By God... surface wells come out, around forty, fifty they
come out... but mostly... many deep wells came... we dug
them near us.

191
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Bahriyê wan da ketine...
 
They have hit the deep ones...

192
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Bahrî çiqas metir da, ava wê çêdike...
 
How many meters for the deep well, does it make its water...

193
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Tegerîban hey e sêsed û pêncî da çêkir. Heye...
 
Approximately there is one created at three hundred and
fifty. There is...

194
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Pirr kur e avê...
 
The water is very deep...

195
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:52,000
Naha em kin e, bîrên kêsên li vî derê bîstan çandine... gişt
bîrê xwe hen e...
 
Now let's see, the people's wells who have planted orchards
here... they all have their own wells...

196
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Gişt bîrê xwe hen e. Êh ti neye, jî... cîranê xwe de avê
dede. Em di wê yekîtir hen e.
 
They all have their own wells. If one doesn't, well... they
give water to their neighbor. We have others there.

197
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Bê hevre alîkariyyê dikin?
 
Do they help each other out?

198
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Nabe, yekî tir...
 
It can't be, another one...

199
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Bîstanê pir aw dikin... naha em dibînin we erd tişt rakirin
dîwarekî çitişt diçînin, Kekê Husên?
 
They water the orchard a lot... now we see you have cleared
the land, what things are you planting, Brother Husên?

200
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Beqdenos (bexdenûs) jî hedi...
 
Parsley as well...

201
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Ah. Yalî, xedrata... ez dixwazim ji mi ra xebere de.
 
Yes. Especially, vegetables... I want you to talk to me
about it.

202
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Şûniyê perêzan, şûna dibên kêmî... meselen heye, zehret,
kelem e (melfûf e) diçîne...
 
The place of the stubbles, the place they call short... for
example there is, cauliflower, they plant cabbage...

203
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Ewa da gîhîne mewsimê payîzê, em tenê?
 
Does that reach the autumn season, only?

204
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Eh we... taqriben, hat e... ber serî salê. Ev we deran
halastin be, gazin.
 
Yes... approximately, it arrives... before the new year. If
these places are clear, they bite.

205
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Yanî, yanî em dibînin... we musmê radikirin dest bi hê din
dikin.
 
Meaning, meaning we see... as you clear the season you start
with the other one.

206
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Ah. Yavaş, yavaş ere... U vakiden genem... ça... evina tişti
livdera da çinan.
 
Yes. Slowly, slowly yes... And earlier the wheat... tea...
they planted these things here.

207
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Tiştî têva de neceyê e yalî Celamê am derên kan naha em bên
Gundî Celame... Arded Gundî muxrafne..
 
If things completely succeed towards Celamê, in our places,
if we now come to the Village of Celamê... the lands of the
Village are well-known..

208
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Bîstana, Bîstana hoca cina cem e, bese tiştî têva rin vera
ta neciha we bîstana we ciya?
 
The orchards, the teacher's orchard goes next to it, but
things run completely towards it, what succeeds in your
orchards?

209
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Û îsot in, Tûtu (Titûn) e... îsot in, melfûf cî dî naha
ciya..
 
And they are peppers, it is Tobacco... they are peppers,
cabbage and what else now..

210
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Û af hê be, gidê maşe.. gidê naşe ara.
 
And if there is water, it's a good place.. it's a place that
doesn't let you down.

211
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Gidê maşe.. erey ci kewe a ra... akeyi..
 
It's a good place.. yes whatever you put in it... it opens..

212
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Xode rizke we bişîn... an pakê xweşen min cîderê wa, te razi
be.. alo sa helo... we kebe le ciridê bi ciyan dar waz be..
gunde ro be..
 
May God send your provision... these clean, beautiful places
of yours, may you be satisfied.. hello.. like you go out
into the field with a stick.. the village is clear..

213
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Edeve gundê da maktab hene?
 
Are there schools in this village?

214
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Mekteb heye.. te cenden ne? Di din ne..
 
There are schools.. how many are they? There are two..

215
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Ez dekozin henke dîxbar seyyid de la, bistavse f, bozor le
we gundê ce dube..
 
I want you to give me a little bit of news about pharmacies,
clinics, how is the market in this village..

216
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Bazar ce de be. seyyide de dest se hene... o bazar ce le ce
debe landa gon mezina .. mezina aa...
 
A market is formed. There are two or three pharmacies... and
a market is formed there, the village is big.. big, yes...

217
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Bozori we gundê, cand şemî şede we? Pêncşemî... Pêncşemî...
 
The market of this village, on which day is it formed?
Thursday... Thursday...

218
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Pêncşemî baad na ce? Baad na cî pêncşemî.
 
Is it formed after Thursday? Also after Thursday.

219
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Seyyid ahan a hem ke da me si seydi der da ahan na? U
makteba we gun ci e han da ge... maktab cihan na ere.
 
Pharmacies yes, so you said there are three pharmacies
right? And the school of this village is there... school is
there yes.

220
00:18:47,000 --> 00:19:00,000
(Silence / ambient sounds)
 
(Silence / ambient sounds)

221
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:20,000
(Silence / ambient sounds)
 
(Silence / ambient sounds)

222
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Keko Hisên, ev titûna hûn çend roj in anîna ber derdixin, û
çi wextan derdixin? Ji me ra agahiyekî bide.
 
Brother Hisên, this tobacco you brought out, how many days
has it been, and when do you bring it out? Give us some
information.

223
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Wextê em biderdixin hêşîn e.
 
When we bring it out, it is green.

224
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Em didin ber tavê viderê hişk dibe.
 
We leave it under the sun here so it dries.

225
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Û paşê di xerbî da em radikin.
 
And then we put it away at sunset.

226
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Di xerbî da?
 
At sunset?

227
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Sibê, berbangê yan?
 
Yes...

228
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Sibê, berbangê yan?
 
In the morning, at dawn?

229
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Sibê zû em bi derdixin.
 
We bring it out early in the morning.

230
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Da ku nerm be, yan ji ber ku hûn naweşînin?
 
So that it stays soft, or because you don't want it to
crumble?

231
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Ji ber ku wê nerm be, em naweşînin wê hûr nabe.
 
So that it stays soft, we don't crumble it so it doesn't
break into small pieces.

232
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Û em dikin... balya paşê.
 
And then we make... bales later.

233
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
Û em radikin, dewletê, hikûmetê.
 
And we store it for the state, the government.

234
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Çend rojan Keko Hisên, ev titûna ko, hûn radikin, çend rojan
dê bikemile, hişk bibe?
 
Brother Hisên, how many days will this tobacco you put away
need to mature and dry?

235
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Teqrîben 20 roj, 25 rojan da hişk dibe.
 
It dries in approximately 20 to 25 days.

236
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:04,000
20 roj, 25 roj ew qas dimîne, hişk dibe.
 
20 days, 25 days it stays like that, it dries.

237
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Di xerbî da em dibin malê.
 
At sunset we take it home.

238
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Da ku... hûr nebe.
 
So that... it doesn't break.

239
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Da ku... hûr nebe û wextê em dest pê dikin wê radikin jî di
dezira dikin, em bi dezira dikin.
 
So that... it doesn't break, and when we start putting it
away, we tie it, we thread it.

240
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:20,000
40 wesle, em 40 pelî, bi hev ra didin hev dikin dezira dikin
vederê, nerm dikin.
 
40 pieces, we string 40 leaves together, thread them here,
make them soft.

241
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,000
20 roj, 25 roj dimîne.
 
It stays for 20 to 25 days.

242
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Di xerbî da em radikin, da ku hûr nebe û em dikin balya
paşê.
 
We take it inside at sunset so it doesn't crumble and then
we make it into bales.

243
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Û paşê em radikin...
 
And then we store it...

244
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Bazirganiyê, ticaretê hûn didin?
 
You sell it to trades, to commerce?

245
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Bazirganiyê, tîcaretê em radikin.
 
We sell it for trades and commerce.

246
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Saeta we xweş... Keko Hisên, titûna Celeme jî heye?
 
Good job... Brother Hisên, is there Celeme tobacco too?

247
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Heye... heye... titûna Celeme heye...
 
Yes... yes... there is Celeme tobacco...

248
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:39,000
Bîrliye, eva...
 
Its name is...

249
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Bîrliye, eva...
 
Burley, this one...

250
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Bîrliye eva. Cûreyê wê hene?
 
This is Burley. Does it have types?

251
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Bîrli heye, berê ya Firnê diçandin. Vê ra dibên Firjînî.
 
There is Burley, in the past they planted oven-dried. They
call it Virginia.

252
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

253
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Eva naha nema, naha kêm bû. Naha bes ev bîrliye, Bîrliye.
 
That is gone now, it's rare now. Now there is only this
burley, Burley.

254
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Hûn ji me balê xwe danê berê li Celeme pir diçandin.
 
You know, we noticed they used to plant a lot in Celeme in
the past.

255
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Pir diçandin, sedî şêst, heştê diçandin berê, bes naha kêm
bûye tişkî.
 
They planted a lot, sixty or eighty percent used to plant,
but now it's a bit less.

256
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Û ji vir û ha da înşeallah wê pir werê çandin.
 
And from now on, God willing, it will be planted a lot.

257
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Û ji vir û ha da, erê... kîjan cûre hebe wê werê çandin.
 
And from now on, yes... whatever type there is will be
planted.

258
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Lema ji vir û ha da dewlet ê teslîm dibe.
 
That's why from now on it's being handed over to the
government.

259
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Ew ê teslîm bibe û wê werê çandin...
 
It will be handed over and it will be planted...

260
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Xwedê quwetê bide we. Rizqê we bixêr û bereket be.
 
May God give you strength. May your livelihood be blessed.

261
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Me xwest em li ser titûnê jî zanibin û me nas kir û bi rastî
me hêşînî jî dît.
 
We wanted to learn about tobacco and we did, and we actually
saw the green fields.

262
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Hêşînî jî dît, ehlen we sehlen.
 
You saw the green fields too, welcome.

263
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,000
Belê pale gihandin hev... ew diçinin û pelên hêşîn dertînin.
 
Yes, the workers gathered... they harvest and pull out the
green leaves.

264
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Pelên gihandin cî, ew dertînin wê dikemile... ew binî va zer
dibe...
 
They harvest the mature leaves, they pull it out so it
ripens... it turns yellow from the bottom.

265
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Pelan digîhînin cî, dîsa av didin, heva jî dikemile û
cîbicî...
 
They arrange the leaves, water them again, this ripens too
and they put it in place.

266
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Sê naqlan avê dertînin ev diçe.
 
They water it three times and this goes.

267
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Sê naql dertînin...
 
They take it out three times...

268
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Ziriyê titûnê jî li cem we heye? Lê yên tînin hişk dibin?
 
Do you have tobacco seeds too? Do the ones you bring dry?

269
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Welle ev ên hêşîn e, wextê bizrê xwe sor dibe... em dizanin
wexta ku wê bikemile...
 
Well, this is the green one, when its seed turns red... we
know when it will mature...

270
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Em wê hildikin û dibin malê... em hema wan nefsê wan bizran
dertînin...
 
We pick it and take it home... we just pull out the very
essence of those seeds.

271
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Hûn eynî wan bizran dertînin.
 
You pull out the exact same seeds.

272
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Saeta we xweş... pir kêfxweş im keko Hisên...
 
Good job... I am very happy Brother Hisên...

273
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Ev jî erdê we ye.
 
Welcome...

274
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Ev jî erdê we ye.
 
This is also your land.

275
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Ev a erdê me ye erê.
 
This is our land, yes.

276
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Xwedê rizqê we, bi zêde bike... û emrê te dirêj be welle...
 
May God increase your livelihood... and may you have a long
life...

277
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Ê te jî dirêj be razî be. Ehlen we sehlen.
 
May yours be long too, be content. Welcome.

278
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Saet xweş Xwedê emrê te dirêj bike û silavê me ji gundê
Celeme tevahî ra.
 
Good job, may God give you a long life, and our greetings to
the entire village of Celeme.

279
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Û înşeelleh em ê her carekê werin...
 
And God willing, we will come every time...

280
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Ehlen we sehlen... kîjan çaxê hûn hatin, ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome... whenever you come, welcome...

281
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Hûn sax bin. Saeta we xweş...
 
Thank you. Good job...

282
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Saeta te jî xweş be. Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Same to you. Welcome...

283
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Saeta we xweş... Xwedê ji we razî be pismamê min, afkê xwere
kin...
 
Good job... May God be pleased with you my cousin, enjoy
your meal...

284
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

285
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Ez pir kêfxweş im bi dîtina we.
 
I am very happy to see you.

286
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Me hûn naskirin pir silavên me bi dil û can hene ji we re...
 
We got to know you, we have many heartfelt greetings for
you...

287
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Em jî gelek kêfxweş bûn bi we. Ehlen we sehlen.
 
We are also very happy with you. Welcome.

288
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,000
Te emrê xwe, we tiştên xwe gotin, em hatin cem we hene...
 
You told us your age, your things, we came to you here...

289
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Sersera, ehlen we sehlen.
 
On my head, welcome.

290
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Keko Hisên saet xweş. Xwedê ji we razî be dayê. Xwedê emrê
te drêj bike dayê.
 
Brother Hisên, good job. May God bless you, mother. May God
give you a long life, mother.

291
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
İnşalleh em ê tim wisa hûn baş û kêfxweş bibînin.
 
God willing, we will always see you well and happy.

292
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Înşelleh ya reb...
 
God willing, oh Lord...

293
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,000
Û em hêjî bînerên me em dewam dikin.. û em xatirê xwe ji we
dixwazin. Qewet ba we, saeta we xweş.
 
And we are still continuing with our viewers.. and we bid
you farewell. Strength be with you, good job.

294
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

295
