Çûm Çûm Efrînê canê, Hatin Efrînê canê.
 
I went, went to Afrin, my dear, They came to Afrin, my dear.

312
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:09,000
Çûm Çûm Efrînê canê, Hatin Efrînê canê.
 
I went, went to Afrin, my dear, They came to Afrin, my dear.

313
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Bînerên me yê ezîz, hûn derbasî gundê Celeme jî bibin, hûn ê
ji bîr nekin, hûn ê derbazî vê Sûkê bibin.
 
Our dear viewers, when you pass by the village of Celeme,
you won't forget it, you will pass by this market.

314
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Ev Sûk jî Sûka Halê ya gundê Celeme ye.
 
And this market is the wholesale market of Celeme village.

315
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Gundê Celeme... hemû kêsên îsotên xwe radikin, dikin
tûran...
 
Celeme village... everyone who harvests their peppers, puts
them in bags...

316
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Piştî wê tînin li vir derê li Sûkê. Ticaret ji vir derê
radibe, em ketin vê navê.
 
After that they bring it here to the market. Trade starts
from here, we have entered this place.

317
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Em li vir derê Sûka Halê dibînin.
 
We are seeing the wholesale market here.

318
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:34,000
Di vê Sûka Halê ya Gundê Celeme da, bes îsot e.
 
In this wholesale market of Celeme village, there are only
peppers.

319
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Û pir kes jî ji van gundan... îsotên xwe dibin Cindirêsê,
dibin Efrînê.
 
And many people from these villages... take their peppers to
Jindires, they take them to Afrin.

320
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Lê da ku hûn em ji nêzîk ve gundî nas bikin. Ka kîjan tişt e
ev gund...
 
But so that you and I can get to know the village closely.
What kind of thing is this village...

321
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Gelê ev gundî bi vê karî radibin.
 
The people of this village undertake this work.

322
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Da ku hûn û em ji nêzîk va nas bikin, bi me ra bin.
 
So that you and I can get to know it closely, stay with us.

323
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Em derbasî cem yekî komîte, rûniştî ye bavekî me ye,
birayekî me ye, em cem wan silav dikin...
 
Let's go to someone in the committee, he is sitting, he is
our father, our brother, we greet them...

324
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Û hinekî em ê bipirsin.
 
And we will ask some questions.

325
00:27:53,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Hela naha hûn li cem me bin da ku em werin cem we... em
derbas bin...
 
Now, stay with us so we can come to you... let's go...

326
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Selamun Eleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

327
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,000
Silav, ehlen wesehlen...
 
Greetings, welcome...

328
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Gelek delal bî...
 
You're very kind...

329
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Delal tu yî, ser serî min.
 
You're kind, on my head.

330
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,000
Sersera...
 
On your head...

331
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Em pir kêfxweş bûn.
 
We were very happy.

332
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,000
Kêfxweş tu bî... Ser seran... Gelek razî me... Ehlen we
sehlen... Xweş hatî...
 
May you be happy... On my head... I am very grateful...
Welcome... Nice to have you here...

333
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Ev a Sûka Halê ya Celeme ye?
 
Is this the wholesale market of Celeme?

334
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:17,000
Erê... Sûka Celeme ye.
 
Yes... It's the market of Celeme.

335
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Me tu nas nekir bira?
 
We didn't get to know you, brother?

336
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Navê min, Hisên Mihemed Hisên. Bi min ra dibêjin Bavê Can.
 
My name is Hisên Mihemed Hisên. They call me Bavê Can.

337
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,000
Bavê Can? Navê Can jî pir xweş e.
 
Bavê Can? The name Can is also very nice.

338
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:25,000
Û can, rehet. Erê Bavê Can.
 
And soul, comfortable. Yes, Bavê Can.

339
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:28,000
Bavê Can ka ji me re... te li ser defterê xwe tiştek
nivîsiye...
 
Bavê Can, tell us... you have written something on your
notebook...

340
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Tu çi dizanî dikî tu tena koma dikî?
 
What things do you know, what do you collect alone?

341
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Welleh evana... evana navê cotkaran e, ez wezin dikim...
 
Well these... these are the names of the farmers, I measure
the weights...

342
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Ev derê jî wezin...
 
That place is the weight...

343
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Cotkar in.. ey tişt me...
 
They are farmers.. things..

344
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Mesela, em dibêjin li vir Welîd Husên e, li vir Cuma, Cemîl,
Silêman e.
 
For example, we say here, it is Welîd Husên, here it is
Cuma, Cemîl, Silêman.

345
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Misto Husên e, mesela Elî Cuma ye, Cemîl Resûl e.
 
Misto Husên... for example, Elî Cuma, Cemîl Resûl.

346
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:49,000
Ez dinivîsim, weznê wî çiqas e. Û eger ku firotinî me jî, ez
bi dolar difiroşim... Dolar...
 
I write down, what their weight is. And if we sell it, I
sell in dollars... dollars...

347
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Em bi xêra dînarê naxebitin.
 
May God reward, we don't work with Dinars.

348
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Her tiştek diçe bi dolar.
 
Everything goes with dollars.

349
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:59,000
Erê naha di vê bazarê da, bes tenê em bi dolar naxebitin,
Tirkî heye, Sûrî heye.
 
Yes now in this market, we don't just work with dollars,
there is Turkish currency, Syrian currency.

350
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Aqilmend ev pere ye.
 
Depending on their minds, their money...

351
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Bi dolar be diçe, derbas bibe naha. Xilas. Xilas şixulê.
 
Pay in dollars, and let it go now. Done. Your work is done.

352
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Bavê Can hemî kesên Gundê Celeme, milkan tînin vî derê?
Riziqê xwe tînin vî derê?
 
Bavê Can, do all the people of Celeme village bring their
goods here? Bring their livelihood here?

353
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Û evên ku li nav vederê, ticaretê cem we ne, bazar..
 
And are these the ones whose trade is with you here, this
market?

354
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Ticareta diçe heya derveyî Sûrî.
 
This trade goes all the way outside of Syria.

355
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Diçin bi Antabê, bi bajar, diçin mesela aliyê şerqê, Ezaz.
 
They go towards Antep, towards the city, they go for example
to the eastern side, Azaz.

356
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Ev ê hemî rê li wê derê kargehên ma'melê hene.
 
They all have their factories and facilities there.

357
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Dikin dims, dikin setlan...
 
They make pepper paste, they put it in buckets...

358
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Di setlan da jî... dikişînin, derdixin...
 
And in buckets... they transport it, send it out...

359
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Derdixin... erê.
 
Send it out... yes.

360
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,000
Kes diçe nav alî Helebê?
 
Aren't there people going towards Aleppo?

361
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Kes diçe nav alî Helebê? Em derbas ne ta tê di Helebê.
 
People going towards Aleppo? No, we don't go to Aleppo now.

362
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Evana jî difiroşin li vî derê, diherin sûka tûran difiroşin
li nav gundan.
 
They also sell these here, go and sell in net bags in the
villages.

363
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Di nav bajarekî de. Wek Sermedê... Danê.. Ev... Gundê din.
 
In a city... like Sarmada, Al-Dana... other villages.

364
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:49,000
Di Menteqê da, mentiqeya Efrînê de merkez Celeme ye.
Celeme...
 
In the region, in the Afrin region, the center is Celeme.
Celeme...

365
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Erê çandiniya îsotan, derecê yekem takrîben li muhafazê
Heleb e.
 
Yes, pepper farming is roughly first degree in the Aleppo
governorate.

